Stop a wrapped prose comment from being parsed as a lint directive

The previous commit's explanatory comment wrapped onto a line beginning with
"# shellcheck to follow...". A comment starting with that word IS a directive,
so the linter tried to parse "to follow." as a key=value pair and failed the
build with SC1072/SC1073 — an error in a comment explaining how to avoid errors
in comments.

Reworded both blocks to say "the linter" in the prose and to reserve the literal
directive word for actual directives, with a note warning the next editor.

No behaviour change: DRY_RUN output and the env-override precedence are
unchanged, and pytest is unaffected.

